}

/* ---------- Depth of field ----------
   Whatever has the focus is sharp; each layer behind it softens by its depth (1 to 3): a breath of
   blur, a little less colour and light, and a window a hair smaller. Barely there on one layer,
   felt on three. A window behind clears halfway under the pointer, to say it can be brought
   forward. The desktop (the conversation, the bar, the box, the docked panels) is the deepest
   layer while a window has the focus; it softens slowly and clears at once when it is touched,
   so nothing it places — a menu, a chip — is ever placed from a blurred box. The one in front
   never carries a filter, for the same reason. */
:is(.tree.window, dialog.surface.window, .conv-window, .browser-dock.window).behind {
